%% State — connection/sync and recommendation lifecycle on main.
%% Sources: backend_api/routers/connections.py, aws_collector/runner.py,
%% optimizer/engine.py, docs/architecture/README.md,
%% docs/architecture/data-pipeline.md, docs/architecture/engines/optimizer.md
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Unsaved: user opens Account Settings
  Unsaved --> Tested: POST /connections/test (STS resolves account)
  Tested --> Unsaved: keys rejected
  Unsaved --> Saved: POST /connections (stored under aws-account_id)
  Tested --> Saved: POST /connections (save after test)
  Saved --> Syncing: POST /connections/{id}/sync (background thread)
  Syncing --> Ready: collect newest-first completes (incremental commits)
  Syncing --> Partial: collector or API failure mid-run
  Partial --> Syncing: re-run sync (clears account data, retries)
  Ready --> Syncing: re-run sync (full replacement per account)
  Ready --> Stale: new months accrue / settings change (no auto re-collect)

  state Recommendations {
    [*] --> Empty: optimize() deletes user rows first
    Empty --> Generated: LP right-sizing + rule checks run
    Generated --> Stored: INSERT into recommendations + COMMIT
    Stored --> Empty: next optimize() run deletes again
  }

  Ready --> Empty: run optimizer for workspace user
